      "id": 4,
      "claim": "A human can survive at most about 7 days (≈168 hours) without water under optimal conditions.",
      "evidence": "Medical literature (WHO, US Army Field Manual) cites 3–5 days typical, with the longest documented cases ≈7 days in cool, low‑activity environments.",
      "weight": 0.20,
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "claim": "The required viewing time (5,500 h) exceeds the maximum survivable time without water (168 h) by more than thirty‑fold.",
      "evidence": "Direct numerical comparison of steps 3 and 4.",
      "weight": 0.15,
      "depends_on": [3, 4]
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "claim": "Therefore it is biologically impossible to binge‑watch the entire EastEnders series without drinking water.",
      "evidence": "If a person must stay alive for the whole viewing period, they would need to survive >5,500 h without water, which far exceeds the physiological limit of ≈168 h.",
      "weight": 0.05,
      "depends_on": [5]
    }
  ],
